\section{Not yet verified}{
The spec records these as open. They are listed rather than hidden:

\itemize{
\item The outcome is mzLib's ComparaColumnOutcome name verbatim (Aligned, GapInTarget, ...), as classify-peptides projects PeptideSharing. genes orthology's statuses are snake_case because mzLib names them (OrthologySnapshot.StatusName). PUSH-TO-MAINLAND: a ComparaGeneTreeAlignment.OutcomeName helper in the same style; when it lands the wire names change to its spelling, a breaking change to call out.
\item MapResidue throws ArgumentOutOfRangeException for a position outside the source, which fails a whole batch. PUSH-TO-MAINLAND: a non-throwing outcome (PositionOutsideSource) so one bad query is one row. Until then the bridge projects the throw and does not check lengths itself.
\item mzLib compares no release between the alignment and the gene-tree content (OrthologySnapshot.Build does, for the dumps). PUSH-TO-MAINLAND: ComparaGeneTreeAlignment.Load could refuse a gene-tree content named for another release, as Build refuses one; the bridge only reports it as a caveat.
\item result.tables (alignment, gene_trees, gene_sets, proteins) is not validated by tools/check_verbs.py, which checks only envelope_fields, columns and bulk. Bridge tests pin each nested object's keys (GenesMapResiduesTests).
\item Not yet ported to mzLibRust or mzLibR; the binding names above are proposals.
}
}
\references{
\itemize{
\item \href{https://doi.org/10.1101/gr.073585.107}{doi:10.1101/gr.073585.107}: Ensembl Compara gene trees, each built on a multiple alignment of its member proteins, the alignment this verb reads columns from (Vilella et al. 2009, Genome Res 19:327)
\item \href{https://doi.org/10.1093/nar/gkaf1239}{doi:10.1093/nar/gkaf1239}: Ensembl releases, their GTFs and the Compara gene-tree files (Ensembl 2026, NAR)
}
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{proteins_align}} for the UniProt legs, \code{\link{proteins_build_orthology}}
}
\examples{

\dontshow{.mzlibr_example <- mzLibR:::replay_bridge_start()}
# A real cut of Ensembl release 116: the TP53 and GAPDH gene trees' alignments, with the human,
# mouse and rat rows exactly as Ensembl publishes them.
gtfs <- c(homo_sapiens = "Homo_sapiens.GRCh38.116.gtf",
          mus_musculus = "Mus_musculus.GRCm39.116.gtf",
          rattus_norvegicus = "Rattus_norvegicus.GRCr8.116.gtf")
site <- proteins_map_residues(list(list("ENSP00000269305", 15, "ENSMUSP00000104298")),
  alignment = "Compara.116.protein_default.aa.fasta.gz",
  gene_trees = "vertebrates.GeneTree_content.default.e116.txt.gz", gtfs = gtfs)
site
# Human p53's Ser15 is mouse p53's Ser18:
site$records[, c("outcome", "column", "target_position", "target_residue")]
c(site$alignment$release, site$gene_trees$collection)
\dontshow{mzLibR:::replay_bridge_stop(.mzlibr_example)}
}
